                alt: "",
                original: "[模範解答1・CEO 報酬 — 朗読] I believe high compensation packages for CEOs at large corporations are justified. I'll discuss attracting top talent, incentives to perform well, and responsibility. The most obvious reason is that competitive salaries are essential to get the best CEOs. ... Therefore, companies need to pay huge salaries to attract CEOs who can come up with innovative and practical business strategies. Then once the CEO has been hired, there has to be an incentive to perform well. While multi-million-dollar salaries may seem like a lot of money, CEOs' compensation is often linked to performance. ... Finally, let's consider responsibility. CEOs carry an incredibly heavy burden. Their decisions affect thousands of workers and involve choices that can make or break the company. It is only fair that they be fairly compensated for the extreme pressure of their jobs. In conclusion, when you look at how important it is to attract the best people, give them incentives, and reward them for their responsibility, it's clear that high compensation packages for CEOs are appropriate.",
                spice: "**★模範解答1の骨 — I believe ~ are justified / I'll discuss A, B, and C / The most obvious reason is that / Therefore / Then once ~ / While ~ may seem like / Finally, let's consider / It is only fair that they be ~ / In conclusion, when you look at how ~, it's clear that ~。**盗む句 — come up with innovative and practical strategies / carry an incredibly heavy burden / make or break the company / fairly compensated。",
