                original: "Uh-huh, yes. Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'm going to steal your words, and. [模範解答3・サイバーセキュリティ — 朗読] Should improving cybersecurity measures be the highest priority for government agencies? Cybersecurity is vital to government agencies, and I strongly believe that enhancing it should be their highest priority. Although government agencies do a lot of essential work, nothing is as urgent as the threat of hackers. If, for example, hackers from a terrorist organization got into the computer systems of water purification plants, dam and flood control systems, or traffic control systems, it could lead to societal chaos and significant loss of life. Therefore, security systems must be upgraded as soon as possible. Second, data leaks are an extremely serious problem. Government computers contain confidential information about every citizen in the country. If this were to fall into the hands of hackers, the information would certainly be misused, resulting in the public's loss of trust in the government. Third, protecting government data is a matter of national security. If foreign nations discover a nation's military secrets, it could allow them to launch attacks on the country. Furthermore, leaks of advanced military technology could change the balance of power in other parts of the world as well. For these reasons, it's clear that governments need to urgently upgrade their cybersecurity.",
