                fix: "Should promoting free trade be a primary goal for the Japanese government? Most economists think free trade is generally a good idea. That mindset is ingrained in us — a growing world economy is always good. That's why we have gadgets like iPhones and state-of-the-art facilities. It all comes from free competition and free trade. So free trade could be an ideal. But the system is rigged. Human nature is to protect what you've already got, and to be afraid of losing it. So the powerful stay powerful. Absolute power corrupts absolutely. I'm not saying rich people are greedy. They were capable of making their millions in the first place, and I'm not dismissing their contribution to society. They pay a lot of tax — there are loopholes, but still, they pay a lot. But we need some kind of system to level the playing field. Because once the gap starts widening, there's no system in today's society to stop it. The rich get richer and the poor get poorer.",
                fixWhy: "**☓free trades → free trade。**数えない名詞。**☓all comes from → IT all comes from。**主語が要る。**☓powerful remains powerful → THE POWERFUL STAY POWERFUL。**the + 形容詞で「〜な人々」(複数扱い)。**☓what they already got → what they'VE already got。**☓I don't disregard their contribution → I'm not DISMISSING their contribution。**「軽く扱うつもりはない」は dismiss。**☓there's no like a system → there's no system。**☓poor people getting poorer and rich people getting richer → THE RICH GET RICHER AND THE POOR GET POORER。**定型は rich が先。",
