                fix: "As the article explains, it didn't work. That's another funny story. That's why I thought, give me one, because I couldn't check the time. But I couldn't ask, because technically I had a watch. The day before — it's weird — I'd bought a cheap analog watch at a dollar store. Like three bucks. And a guy wearing a watch can't exactly put his hand up and ask for one. So the test started. Right at 2 p.m., I set my watch — and I'd already noticed this watch was done. But I'm kind of a crazy guy, so I still believed in my cheap watch. It didn't work. At least I had that under control — or so I thought. The room was so hot. Twenty-something people, all nervous, no air. My brain overheated — it really happened. In about 30 minutes, my CPU was totally fried. I looked around, and surprisingly, no one else was sweating. Just me. Everybody else was calm and cool, and I was the guy who'd walked for an hour and a half. Maybe that was the cause. Then I checked my watch: 2:20. Okay, only twenty minutes in. I've got plenty of time. I kept going for a while and checked again. It felt like at least half an hour had gone by, but my watch was going so slowly.",
